{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfVDSEYQpEShxTa5ukmid","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 11 is complete. Recap:\n\n**What was built.** `learning/bound_harness.py` takes any candidate lower bound as a Python function and runs it through three checks: validity on every certified instance with the \"above optimum (must be 0)\" column and counterexample drawing, an extremal-search attack with the exact solver as oracle, and tightness on the 338 gap instances against the reference `max(lb_best, tw + 1)`. Three candidates went through it: the plan's recursive cut-vertex branch rule, a separator generalisation (Lemma A, proved in §38 by the layout argument), and the same rule over the contraction-degeneracy minors.\n\n**What it found.**\n- All three candidates are valid on all 49,862 certified instances evaluated (corpus and campaign complete; upward 5,686 of 6,773, said so in the report) and survive 11,880 adversarial evaluations each, reaching the optimum in every job without crossing it.\n- None beats the reference on a gap instance by branching. `contract-branch` is above it on 8 (2.4%), all from a minor's treewidth seed where the reference's treewidth is a 1-second interval.\n- The branch rule itself adds at most one stack, on 0.1 to 0.3% of rows, always where pathwidth equals treewidth plus one, and always tight there (forests, sparse trees of cliques). On the 5,003 exact-treewidth rows where pathwidth exceeds treewidth, the candidates are tight on 1.2%.\n- Kill criterion met: the gap stacks are not recoverable by the branch rule at any separator the clique structure exposes.\n\n**Deliverables.** §38 in `reports/ml_nature.md`, tables in `reports/bound_harness_tables.md`, data under `learning/data/ensemble/` (values, two attack files, logs), 14 tests in `tests/test_bound_harness.py`. Full suite: 1,214 passed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed on the final code. `solutions/` untouched, no solver default changed, nothing committed. PROGRESS.md has the iteration entry (11/13 solved) and item 11 is marked done in iterations.md.\n\n**Next** is item 12, the remaining tree-decomposition gaps in `Sandwich.lean`; Lemma A's proof in §38 is the separator form of the branch lemma it needs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2292,"cache_read_input_tokens":278372,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2292,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a52edca2-4c69-48c7-afaf-e25fb647f52b","uuid":"d10128f0-52a9-466a-b6a7-e2828a69c935","timestamp":"2026-09-28T04:35:24.495Z","request_id":"req_011CfVDSDo2HF3oqQhfLFs9B"}
